{"nodes": [{"id": "contributing_browser_only_editing", "label": "Browser-Only Editing Workflow", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The guide is for the committee, not programmers: nothing is installed, everything happens on github.com. A wrong change is one click to revert, and a change that breaks the build is refused rather than published."}, {"id": "contributing_publish_bulletin", "label": "Publish the Bulletin", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "contributing_add_gallery_photos", "label": "Add Photos to the Gallery", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Upload and commit; there is no list to update. A new album needs only a folder plus one entry in albums.yaml whose id matches the folder name."}, {"id": "contributing_photo_size_limit", "label": "2000px Photo Size Limit", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Straight-from-the-phone photos turn a thirty-second build into ten minutes and will eventually make it fail, because every image is processed at build time."}, {"id": "contributing_filename_ordering", "label": "Filename-Ordered Gallery Photos", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Photos render in filename order, so 01-, 02-, 03- prefixes are the whole ordering mechanism; no index file to keep in sync."}, {"id": "contributing_committee_roster_edit", "label": "Update the Committee Roster", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The entire roster is one YAML file with a fixed role vocabulary; names are written once and shown in both languages while roles and ministry names translate automatically."}, {"id": "contributing_event_authoring", "label": "Add or Edit an Event", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "contributing_page_file_map", "label": "Page-to-File Map", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "contributing_build_failure_recovery", "label": "When the Build Fails", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A failed build keeps serving the previous working version, so nothing is broken for visitors; the error names the file and the field, and Revert is the escape hatch."}, {"id": "contributing_before_launch_todo", "label": "Before Launch TODO List", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "contributing_locale_path_helpers", "label": "localePath and assetPath Helpers", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never hand-write an internal href: the site is deployed both at / (Cloudflare) and /CUTES/ (GitHub Pages), so a hard-coded /en/... works on one and 404s on the other with no error in the build log. These are the only functions where a bug bre